{
	title: 'Tools as files',
	description: 'Every model tool is one file in src/host/tools/, named like the tool (read.ts, bash.ts), found by listing the directory the way src/host/commands.ts finds slash commands, so adding a tool touches nothing else. Each file exports `tool`: its definition (name, description, parameters), readOnly when running it changes nothing (task wb), and run(input, ctx). src/host/tools.ts keeps only the registry: listing, provider definitions, dispatch, readOnly lookup. Tools run one after another in call order, as now: later tools (spawn then wait) rely on it.',
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['1r'],
	foldInto: ['sj', '1r']
}
